PHONEBRIDGE — ROBUST COMMUNICATION & DELIVERY ENGINE

ROLE

Act as a senior distributed systems engineer, Android engineer, security engineer, backend architect, and reliability engineer.

Design and implement the complete production-minded communication and event-delivery infrastructure for PhoneBridge, a private, one-way Android notification bridge between two personally owned Android devices.

The Primary device (Tecno) captures selected events and sends them to the Secondary device (Samsung).

The Secondary receives, securely stores, acknowledges, and presents those events.

This assignment focuses specifically on the communication, synchronization, reliability, security, persistence, and recovery layer.

Do not build a superficial networking demo.

Build a real, maintainable, testable system designed for unreliable mobile networks, Android background restrictions, device restarts, temporary server outages, duplicate delivery, and offline devices.

---

1. SYSTEM OBJECTIVE

Implement a robust one-way event-delivery infrastructure that guarantees the best achievable delivery reliability under Android and network constraints.

The system must prioritize:

1. Durable event persistence.
2. Reliable delivery.
3. End-to-end encryption.
4. Deduplication.
5. Offline recovery.
6. Reconnection.
7. Synchronization.
8. Event integrity.
9. Device authentication.
10. Battery efficiency.
11. Privacy.
12. Observability without sensitive logging.

The system must not depend on both phones being connected to the same Wi-Fi network.

It must support phones operating across different mobile networks and internet connections.

The Primary must never be remotely controlled by the Secondary.

The Secondary may send transport acknowledgements, synchronization requests, and protocol-level messages necessary for delivery, but no operational commands controlling the Primary.

