4. EVENT DELIVERY MODEL

Implement an at-least-once delivery system with idempotent processing.

Do not promise mathematically perfect exactly-once delivery.

Achieve effectively-once event presentation by implementing deduplication at the Primary, Relay, and Secondary layers.

Every event must have a unique immutable identifier.

Use a cryptographically secure UUID or another appropriate globally unique identifier.

Every event must have a sequence number assigned by the Primary.

Event identifiers and sequence numbers must be preserved throughout the delivery pipeline.

