13. SYNCHRONIZATION CURSOR

Implement a robust cursor system.

The Secondary should maintain its last successfully processed synchronization position.

The cursor must not advance beyond events that have not been durably processed.

The system must handle:

- Out-of-order events.
- Missing sequence numbers.
- Duplicate events.
- Pagination.
- Interrupted sync.
- Relay restart.
- Secondary restart.
- Event expiration.
- Concurrent incoming WebSocket events.

Define precisely how cursors work and how they are recovered.

Do not assume a single global cursor is sufficient unless the protocol guarantees that it is.

Use an appropriate per-device or per-relationship synchronization model.

